{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating decision (perception) states from action (commit) states. The specification enforces safe, coverage-biased exploration: forward/random_walk in clear, conservative recovery on obstacles, and rapid return to exploration after recovery. Each obstacle event leads to a dedicated recovery state with a single safe controllable, and all uncontrollable events are handled in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (decision) states from action (commit/recovery) states to reflect open-loop pulse semantics and ensure safety under uncontrollable events.",
    "Specification enforces: (1) only safe controllable actions per state, (2) rapid return to exploration after recovery, (3) no forward/random_walk in obstacle states, (4) full_rotate only as last-resort recovery."
  ],
